[center][size=6][b][color=#b78ae8]A D A M A N T[/color][/b][/size]
[size=4][i]Build something the horde cannot take back.[/i][/size]

[img]%%IMG_HERO%%[/img][/center]

A near-indestructible building block and spike trap for [b]7 Days to Die V3.0 and V3.1[/b], with a custom purple crystalline texture. Zombies can't touch it. Neither can bullets, sledgehammers, or a demolisher going off in your face. Only your tools can.

[center][color=#b78ae8]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#b78ae8]The Block[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Zero damage[/b] from zombies, animals, explosions, and player [b]weapons[/b] (guns and melee alike).
[*][b]Only mineable with tools[/b]: pickaxe, axe, auger, shovel, nailgun, salvage tool.
[*][b]10x steel stability[/b] and full explosion immunity, so demolishers do nothing.
[*]Custom [b]adamant[/b] texture on the full shape set, added to the block atlas by the mod itself.
[/list]

[center][img]%%IMG_SHAPES%%[/img][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#b78ae8]The Spike Trap[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]60 damage per hit[/b], where vanilla iron spikes deal 33.
[*][b]It never wears out.[/b] Iron spikes take damage every time they hurt something and break after about six hits. These take none, ever.
[*]Same protection as the block: immune to zombies, weapons and explosions, and [b]demolisher-proof[/b] (they don't stomp it like normal spikes).
[*]Slows whatever walks into it, and you can pick it back up with a tool.
[/list]

[quote]Traps share a damage cooldown of 1.5s per target, so stacking more spikes doesn't multiply damage. A deeper field buys you [i]time[/i], not DPS. Plan the maze accordingly.[/quote]

[center][img]%%IMG_TRAPS%%[/img][/center]

[center][color=#b78ae8]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#b78ae8]Requirements[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Tested on game versions 3.0.0, 3.0.1 and 3.1.0.[/b] Those are the builds this release was actually launched and verified on. Other 3.x versions may work, but they are untested.
[*][b]No other mods required.[/b] The custom texture is added to the block atlas by this mod itself - no core mod, no paint framework, nothing else to install or keep updated.
[*][b]EasyAntiCheat must be off[/b]: this mod ships a Harmony DLL. Single-player and private servers.
[*][b]Multiplayer:[/b] install on both client and server.
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#b78ae8]Two Editions[/color][/b][/size]
[b]Install one, not both.[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Survival[/b] (main file): earn it. Rare ore, a real crafting chain.
[*][b]Creative[/b] (optional file): 1 wood, straight from the backpack. For builders and testing.
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#b78ae8]Survival Crafting Chain[/color][/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*][b]Adamant Ore[/b] — roughly a 4% chance while harvesting iron, lead or coal ore veins.
[*][b]Adamant Ingot[/b] (workbench) — 25 Forged Steel + 20 Concrete Mix + 10 Scrap Polymers + 5 Scrap Lead + 1 Adamant Ore.
[*][b]Adamant Block[/b] (workbench) — 1 Adamant Ingot.
[*][b]Adamant Spikes Trap[/b] (workbench) — 2 Adamant Ingots. Harvesting one gives an ingot back.
[/list]
The Forged Steel already requires a crucible forge, so the ingot stays a mid-to-late game project.

[center][img]%%IMG_CRAFTING%%[/img][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#b78ae8]Installation[/color][/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install one edition's zip with Vortex or MO2, or extract its folder into [i]7 Days To Die/Mods/[/i].
[*]Launch with EAC disabled.
[/list]

[center][color=#b78ae8]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#b78ae8]Changelog[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3][b]1.2.1[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Fixed:[/b] some paints from other mods showed the adamant texture instead of their own. Nothing was saved wrong — update and restart, and they look right again.
[/list]
[size=3][b]1.2.0[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]No extra mod needed any more.[/b] Adamant used to need the OcbCustomTextures core mod just to show its texture. It brings its own now — one less thing to install and keep updated.
[*][b]Adamant is no longer in the paint tool[/b], on purpose. The old way left an entry in your save that could point at the wrong texture whenever you added or removed other paint mods, and in bad cases that broke loading the world. Blocks you have already built are unaffected.
[*]If the texture ever fails to load, the block now looks like plain steel instead of looking broken, and everything else still works.
[/list]
[size=3][b]1.1.0[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]New:[/b] Adamant Spikes Trap. Hits almost twice as hard as iron spikes, never wears out, and demolishers can't stomp it.
[*][b]Fixed:[/b] Adamant Ingots could be made for free, one at a time. They are crafted at the workbench now and cost what they should.
[/list]
[size=3][b]1.0.0[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]First release for 7 Days to Die V3.0.
[/list]
[i]Full history: [url=https://github.com/HannaPanda/7D2D-Adamant/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md]CHANGELOG.md[/url] on GitHub.[/i]

